From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Illia Komsa <kamsaaa@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:13:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] karouka: embed LibWeb in one process for the karouka renderer

All of karouka's changes to Ladybird, squashed into one commit on top of
upstream 1a9bd18fc433dc187252fc9014c43b837d3a98fb. They make LibWeb usable
as an in-process, network-free HTML-to-texture renderer and Python module:

- CMake: an out-of-tree hook (KAROUKA_SOURCE_DIR) that builds karouka's
  sources against the Lagom objects; the browser, its services and their
  vcpkg dependencies are left out of pruned builds.
- Loading: ResourceLoader without a RequestServer, in-place document loads,
  no LibTLS, disk cache, HSTS preload list, libpsl or OpenSSL in the link.
- Images: AVIF decoding (libavif, dav1d, libyuv) is optional
  (LADYBIRD_AVIF), and off in karouka builds.
- Pruning: options that leave out Web API families a UI layer doesn't need
  (IndexedDB, WebSockets, WebDriver, Service Workers, WebGL, WebAssembly,
  SubtleCrypto, Notifications, MSE/Media Capture, ...), and the bindings
  generator prunes union alternatives to match.
- Embedder hooks: a host clock for timers, animations and Date reads, a
  font provider for system UI families, script types for
  <script type="text/python">, off-thread compile waits, idle collection of
  stage-thread heaps, and halting background threads.
- Rendering: drawing a PaintingSurface into a Metal texture, Metal device
  selection without the window server, opacity-layer folding and bounds.
- Layout and memory: layout only when something invalidated it, lazy
  font-family lists and counter styles, less CSS parser churn, trimmed ICU
  and libxml2, mimalloc purge fixes.
- Fixes to bidi text order, grid abspos alignment, clip-path geometry boxes
  and wheel-gesture latching.
